\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IG}{\texttt{Stacks tag 09IG}}
\group{algebra}

Let $A$ be a Noetherian domain of dimension $1$ with fraction field $K$.
Let $L/K$ be a finite extension. Let $B$ be the
integral closure of $A$ in $L$. Then $B$ is a Dedekind domain and
$\Spec(B) \to \Spec(A)$ is surjective, has finite fibres, and
induces finite residue field extensions.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
\uses{algebra-lemma-krull-akizuki, algebra-lemma-integral-sub-dim-equal, algebra-lemma-characterize-Dedekind, algebra-lemma-integral-overring-surjective, algebra-lemma-finite-extension-residue-fields-dimension-1}

By Krull-Akizuki (Lemma \ref{algebra-lemma-krull-akizuki})
the ring $B$ is Noetherian. By Lemma \ref{algebra-lemma-integral-sub-dim-equal}
$\dim(B) = 1$. Thus $B$ is a Dedekind domain by
