Suppose that we have ring maps $A \to A'$ and $A \to B$.
Set $B' = B \otimes_A A'$, so that we obtain a diagram as above.
Then the canonical map defined above
induces an isomorphism
$\Omega^\bullet_{B/A} \otimes_A A' = \Omega^\bullet_{B'/A'}$
of complexes.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
\uses{algebra-lemma-differentials-base-change}

This follows from Lemma \ref{algebra-lemma-differentials-base-change}
and the fact that taking exterior powers commutes with base change.
