\begin{lemma}[Homotopy shift cochain]
\label{homology-lemma-homotopy-shift-cochain}
\source{stacks:011I}
\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/011I}{\texttt{Stacks tag 011I}}
\group{homology}

Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive category.
Suppose that $A^\bullet$ and $B^\bullet$ are
cochain complexes. Given any morphism of cochain
complexes $a : A^\bullet \to B^\bullet$ there
is a bijection between the set of homotopies
