there exists an arrow $s : X \to X'$ in $S$ such that $X'$ computes
$RF$, then $RF$ is everywhere defined.
\item If for every object $X \in \Ob(\mathcal{D})$
there exists an arrow $s : X' \to X$ in $S$ such that $X'$ computes
